# Array alias mutation preserves value semantics

Verifies mutating an array copied into another binding uses copy-on-write, so
the original keeps its element while the copy observes the replacement.

>>> source
let original: int[] = [10, 20]
let copy = original
copy[0] = 99
print(original[0])
print(copy[0])

<<< stdout
10
99

<<< stderr
